WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.420
Metamorphism changes solid rock. Grains recrystallize, grow, or react

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.800
to form new minerals. If rock melts, that part

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.000
of its history follows an igneous pathway. Near an

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.780
intrusion, heating can occur without much additional burial. Regional

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.320
burial can increase pressure and temperature. A cool subducting

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.080
slab reaches high pressure at lower temperature than surrounding

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.580
deep crust. Read both axes. Active fluids move through

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.900
pores and fractures, adding or removing components. Parent composition

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.600
controls which minerals can form. Minerals and fabrics constrain

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.840
the history, but grade and tectonic setting require several

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:38.780
pieces of evidence.
